{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778377069432,"sessionID":"ses_1f077e03fffem0uI8sxyktJpDA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_7IbcBSZwNScLSfjqyOTJjAFp","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"AnnotationAssertion\\(rdfs:label obo:RO_0002203|RO_0002203|develops directly into|develops from","path":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","include":"cl-edit.owl"},"output":"Found 50 matches\n/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl:\n  Line 3890: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D013090\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000017 \"A male germ cell that develops from spermatogonia. The euploid primary spermatocytes undergo meiosis and give rise to the haploid secondary spermatocytes which in turn give rise to spermatids.\")\n\n  Line 3902: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D013087\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000018 \"A male germ cell that develops from the haploid secondary spermatocytes. Without further division, spermatids undergo structural changes and give rise to spermatozoa.\")\n\n  Line 3915: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D013094\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000019 \"A mature male germ cell that develops from a spermatid.\")\n\n  Line 4347: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0618947256\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000058 \"Skeletogenic cell that is typically non-terminally differentiated, secretes an avascular, GAG rich matrix; is not buried in cartilage tissue matrix, retains the ability to divide, located adjacent to cartilage tissue (including within the perichondrium), and develops from prechondroblast (and thus prechondrogenic) cell.\")\n\n  Line 4376: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0618947256\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000060 \"Skeletogenic cell that secretes dentine matrix, is derived from the odontogenic papilla, and develops from a preodontoblast cell.\")\n\n  Line 4391: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781733901\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000061 \"Skeletogenic cell that produces cementum (a bony substance that covers the root of a tooth), is part of the odontogenic papilla, and develops from a precementoblast cell.\")\n\n  Line 5055: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23616747\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000129 \"Unlike macroglial cells, microglial cells  arise from hematopoietic stem cells in the yolk sac during early embryogenesis that populate the central nervous system. They derive from embryonic mesoderm and are not from neuroectoderm where glioblast develops from. Markers: Mouse: CD11b+, F4/80+, CD68+. They represent ~12% of the cells in the CNS, but they are not uniformly distributed within the CNS. A normal adult mouse brain has approximately 3.5x10e6 microglia. Microglia are also reportedly CD3-negative, CD4-positive, CD8-negative, CD11b-positive, CD11c-high, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD45-low, CD56-negative, CD163-negative, CD200R-positive, CD281-positive, CD282-positive, CD283-positive, CD284-positive, CD285-positive, CD286-positive, CD287-positive, CD288-positive, CD289-positive, Gr1-negative, nestin-positive, and PU.1-positive.\")\n\n  Line 5118: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20303382\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20305780\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29286323\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31473260\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32084275\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9177213\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1186/1755-1536-5-S1-S6\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000135 \"A bone marrow-derived cell that predominantly develops from myeloid lineage-restricted progenitor cells and circulates in peripheral blood, characterized by co-expression of hematopoietic markers CD45 and CD34 along with stromal markers including collagen type I in both humans and mice (Chesney et al., 1997; Blakaj and Bucala, 2012). This spindle-shaped cell exhibits a unique dual identity, functionally bridging immune and stromal compartments with characteristics of both monocytes and fibroblasts. Predominantly arising from circulating monocytes, it migrates to injury sites via chemokine receptors and participates in wound repair through extracellular matrix deposition, cytokine secretion, and antigen presentation via MHC class II. As mesenchymal progenitors, fibrocytes can differentiate into fibroblasts, myofibroblasts, and adipocytes, contributing to both physiological repair and pathological fibrosis (Blakaj and Bucala, 2012).\")\n\n  Line 5159: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D019902\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32491508\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000138 \"A skeletogenic cell that secretes a specialized, avascular, GAG-rich matrix, is embedded in cartilage tissue matrix, retains the ability to divide, and develops from a chondroblast cell.\")\n\n  Line 6881: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D014327\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37630754\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1007/978-3-030-84725-8\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000351 \"An extraembryonic cell that develops from a trophectodermal cell. This cell is found in the outer layer of the blastocyst and can invade other structures in the uterus once the blastocyst implants into the uterine wall. A trophoblast cell is involved in the implantation of the embryo into the uterine wall, placental formation, remodelling of maternal vasculature in the uterus, nutrient and gas exchange, hormone production, and immune modulation to support fetal development.\")\n\n  Line 6975: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000363 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0000081 from Plant Ontology instead. OBSOLETE, use term from the Plant Ontology. A secondary vascular cell that develops from the fusiform cambial initials and oriented with their longest diameter parallel with the main axis of stem or root. These cells make up the axial system, also known as vertical or longitudinal system.\")\n\n  Line 6982: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000364 \"Obsolete. Consult Plant Ontology. A cell that develops from the ray initial and composes all rays (panels of tissue variable in height and width, formed by the ray initials in the vascular cambium and extending radially in the secondary xylem and secondary phloem) in the secondary vascular tissues.\")\n\n  Line 8115: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000513 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001133) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002203 obo:CL_0000746)))\n\n  Line 8125: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000514 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002203 obo:CL_0000192)))\n\n  Line 8133: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000515 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002203 obo:CL_0008002)))\n\n  Line 8662: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000569 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0008019 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002203 obo:CL_0002494)))\n\n  Line 8871: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D008184\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000590 \"A progesterone secreting cell in the corpus luteum that develops from theca cells.\")\n\n  Line 8889: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D008184\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000592 \"A large, progesterone secreting cell in the corpus luteum that develops from the granulosa cells.\")\n\n  Line 9136: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000621 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002203 obo:CL_0008003))\n\n  Line 9692: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000680 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0011115 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002203 obo:CL_0000187)))\n\n  Line 11518: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000857 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002203 obo:CL_0000189)))\n\n  Line 11524: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000858 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002203 obo:CL_0000190)))\n\n  Line 11543: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ana\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15771589\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000861 \"A macrophage which develops from an inflammatory monocyte and is recruited into the tissues in response to injury and infection as part of an inflammatory response. Markers include CD11b-positive, CD68-positive, and F4/80-positive.\")\n\n  Line 12441: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19416870\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33352411\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000940 \"An alpha-beta T cell that is found in the lamina propria of mucosal tissues and is restricted by the MR-1 molecule. This cell develops from double-positive, alpha-beta thymocyte.\")\n\n  Line 12672: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:msz\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9280752\") obo:IA