 reference to the quiescent granulosa cells that surround the primordial ovarian follicle, while a pre-granulosa cell proliferates to form the primordial follicle (and thus cells become the squamous granulosa cells).\")\n32983: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033083 \"squamous granulosa cell\")\n32984: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033083 obo:CL_0000501)\n32985: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033083 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0003981))\n32986: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033083 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002207 obo:CL_4033066))\n32987: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033083 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002210 obo:CL_4033084))\n32988: \n32989: # Class: obo:CL_4033084 (cuboidal granulosa cell)\n32990: \n32991: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28892263\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033084 \"A granulosa cell that has a cuboidal morphology and develops from squamous granulosa cell during the transition between primordial follicle to primary follicle. Cuboidal granulosa cells proliferate to form a second layer within secondary follicles.\")\n32992: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033084 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32993: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033084 \"2024-09-24T13:14:57Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32994: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19001500\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033084 \"columnar granulosa cell\")\n32995: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31849844\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033084 \"cuboidal epithelial granulosa cell\")\n32996: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19001500\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033084 \"columnar GC\")\n32997: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33914868\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033084 \"cuboidal GC\")\n32998: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033084 \"cuboidal gra